## Agent tooling (local scratch — configuration, caches and session state, not source)
#
# Every entry below is a directory an assistant creates in the repository root while working. They are
# machine-local: they hold per-user settings, cached indexes and transcripts of sessions, and two
# contributors running the same tools produce different contents for the same commit. Left untracked
# they are worse than noise — a single `git add -A` sweeps them into a commit, and they are the files
# most likely to carry an absolute home path or a key.
#
# Ignored rather than deleted: the tools recreate them, and a contributor who does not use them never
# sees one. If any of this ever becomes shared project configuration, un-ignore that one path
# deliberately with a `!` rule rather than dropping the block.
.agents/
.atl/
.claude/
.kiro/
.superpowers/
.mcp.json
skills-lock.json
backups/
